      "proposition": "The Clean Air Act's allocation of interstate-emissions regulation to EPA and source States preempts Colorado tort claims whose theory of injury necessarily depends on aggregate out-of-state and international greenhouse-gas emissions; displacement of federal common law did not give a downwind State authority to impose that liability."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The holding will be limited to claims, as pleaded, that use global climate injury to impose damages for interstate and international fossil-fuel production and sales, without categorically immunizing locally deceptive marketing or deciding claims confined to in-state conduct or source-state law."
    }
